IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `baominh-par-cover`

-- Bao Minh property all risks rules: THE EXCLUSIONS (src:27-248).
-- Layer 1 of 3, continued: "do bất kỳ nguyên nhân nào không bị hợp đồng bảo hiểm loại trừ".
--
-- HOW CAUSATION IS READ (NOTES.md fork F3). Each damaged item carries its chain of causation:
-- a list of links, each a cause, whether it acted DIRECTLY on the item, and whether it itself
-- followed from earlier Damage by another cause. The document uses three causal phrasings and
-- this module keeps them apart:
--   * "gây ra bởi" (caused by), exclusions 1, 6, 8(f)-(h), 10: a DIRECT link only;
--   * "gây ra bởi hay phát sinh từ" (caused by or arising from), exclusions 2 and 5: ANY link;
--   * "trực tiếp hoặc gián tiếp ..." with "bất kể có nguyên nhân hoặc sự kiện nào khác",
--     exclusions 3, 4, 10(a)(i) and 11: ANY link, whatever else contributed.
--
-- WHAT AN EXCLUSION DOES TO AN ITEM is one of three things (`The effect of the exclusions on an
-- item`): nothing; exclude the Damage to it; or exclude it except for "phần Tổn hại phát sinh
-- từ" a cause not excluded (exclusions 1(a), 1(c) and 8(h)). Exclusion 9 (marine) leaves the
-- excess over the marine policy, and is applied in the quantum module.

§ `The exclusions`
-- src:27 | LOẠI TRỪ
-- src:28 | Đơn bảo hiểm này sẽ không bảo hiểm

§§ `Helpers: the chain of causation`

GIVEN i IS A `A damaged item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A link in the chain of causation`
`the direct links of` i MEANS
    filter (GIVEN k YIELD k's `direct`) (i's `the chain of causation`)

-- A direct link's cause is one of the causes listed.
GIVEN i  IS A `A damaged item`
      cs IS A LIST OF `A cause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a direct cause of the Damage to` i `is one of` cs MEANS
    any (GIVEN k YIELD elem (k's `the cause`) cs) (`the direct links of` i)

-- Any link's cause, direct or indirect, is one of the causes listed.
GIVEN i  IS A `A damaged item`
      cs IS A LIST OF `A cause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`any cause of the Damage to` i `is one of` cs MEANS
    any (GIVEN k YIELD elem (k's `the cause`) cs) (i's `the chain of causation`)

§§ `The facts some exclusions need, and the refusals when they are missing`

@ref exclusion 1(c)(i) (src:48-49): whether the theft was in the insured building, with force or violence
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the circumstances of the theft are not in the record` MEANS
    REFUSE "the circumstances of the theft are not in the record"

@ref exclusion 1(c)(vi) (src:57-58): whether the insured building was empty or not in use
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`whether the insured building was empty or not in use is not in the record` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether the insured building was empty or not in use is not in the record"

@ref exclusion 3(c) (src:83-89): the facts that make an act terrorism
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the facts about the act of force or violence are not in the record` MEANS
    REFUSE "the facts about the act of force or violence are not in the record"

@ref exclusion 3 d), the proviso (src:98-100): when the Damage happened relative to the dispossession
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`when the Damage happened, relative to the dispossession, is not in the record` MEANS
    REFUSE "when the Damage happened, relative to the dispossession, is not in the record"

