GIVETH A LIST OF `A cause`
`the causes named in exclusion 1(c) without a condition` MEANS
    LIST `a fraudulent or dishonest act`
       , `unexplained disappearance`
       , `inventory shortage`
       , `an unknown cause`
       , `an error in recording information`
       , `a shortage in the supply or delivery of materials`
       , `an administrative or accounting error`
       , `cracking, fracture, collapse or overheating of a boiler, economiser, vessel or pipe`
       , `leakage of a boiler weld`
       , `mechanical or electrical breakdown or derangement of machinery or equipment`

-- (i): theft is excluded UNLESS it happened in the insured building AND force or violence was
-- used to break in or to get out.
@ref exclusion 1(c)(i) (src:48-49)
GIVEN l IS A `A loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the theft falls under exclusion 1(c)(i)` l MEANS
    CONSIDER l's `the theft`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the circumstances of the theft are not in the record`
    WHEN JUST t  THEN NOT (    t's `in the insured building`
                           AND t's `with force or violence to break in or to get out`)

-- (vi): bursting, overflowing or leaking of water tanks, pipes or apparatus, only while the
-- insured building is empty or not in use.
@ref exclusion 1(c)(vi) (src:57-58)
GIVEN l IS A `A loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the escape of water falls under exclusion 1(c)(vi)` l MEANS
    CONSIDER l's `the insured building was empty or not in use`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `whether the insured building was empty or not in use is not in the record`
    WHEN JUST e  THEN e

@ref exclusion 1(c)(i)-(vi) (src:48-58)
GIVEN l IS A `A loss`
      c IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cause falls under exclusion 1(c)` l c MEANS
    BRANCH IF c EQUALS theft
           THEN `the theft falls under exclusion 1(c)(i)` l
           IF c EQUALS `bursting, overflowing or leaking of water tanks, pipes or apparatus`
           THEN `the escape of water falls under exclusion 1(c)(vi)` l
           OTHERWISE elem c `the causes named in exclusion 1(c) without a condition`

